      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786292043300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. All IT load is continuous. A 30 A circuit gives 24\nA, and the conductor is sized to the same 125 % - see\nE-430.",
      "originalText": "1. All IT load is continuous. A 30 A circuit gives 24 A, and the conductor is sized to the same 125 % - see E-430.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 189,
      "versionNonce": 1928362886,
      "index": "b5B",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e385",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1470.4946128839315,
      "y": 845.8682699448202,
      "width": 384.5858132254943,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786292043300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Line currents here are summed arithmetically per\nline, which is the conservative direction for line-to-\nline loads. The vector sum on a balanced panel is\nlower.",
      "originalText": "2. Line currents here are summed arithmetically per line, which is the conservative direction for line-to-line loads. The vector sum on a balanced panel is lower.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 214,
      "versionNonce": 128129734,
      "index": "b5C",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e386",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1470.4946128839315,
      "y": 908.8682699448202,
      "width": 382.0381858609197,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786292043300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Do not derive the feeder from the sum of the\nbreakers. It is derived from the calculated load -\nhere the failover case, 67.2 A, at 125 %.",
      "originalText": "3. Do not derive the feeder from the sum of the breakers. It is derived from the calculated load - here the failover case, 67.2 A, at 125 %.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 222,
      "versionNonce": 54514182,
      "index": "b5D",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e387",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1470.4946128839315,
      "y": 964.8682699448202,
      "width": 392.22903119625977,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786292043300,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Available fault current and series ratings come from\nthe utility and the study, not from this sheet. Mark\nthe panel with the available fault current per NEC\n110.24.",
      "originalText": "4. Available fault current and series ratings come from the utility and the study, not from this sheet. Mark the panel with the available fault current per NEC 110.24.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
